WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.168
A discarded sofa, a mattress, and tires left by the curb. Imagine a

00:00:04.168 --> 00:00:08.399
resident opens a San José three one one report. How many new illegal

00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:11.572
dumping reports will reach this district next week?

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:16.816
Follow District Three. The four previous weeks brought one hundred fifteen,

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:21.296
one hundred sixty-nine, one hundred sixteen, and one hundred twenty-one

00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:25.018
reports. Their weekly average was about one hundred thirty.

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:30.066
Before Monday, July twenty ninth, the Poisson model used recent counts,

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:34.611
four and thirteen week averages, the district, and the time of year. Its

00:00:34.611 --> 00:00:37.894
forecast was about one hundred twenty-three reports.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:42.464
By Sunday, the district had received two hundred twenty-seven reports.

00:00:42.464 --> 00:00:46.686
Orange shows the observed surge on the same scale. About one hundred four

00:00:46.686 --> 00:00:49.288
more reports arrived than the model expected.

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:54.131
Now the virtual street is anchored to a marker on a photographed tabletop.

00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:58.313
As the image moves, the miniature stays on the marker. This is augmented

00:00:58.313 --> 00:01:02.553
reality. The streetscape illustrates the problem. The forecast and report

00:01:02.553 --> 00:01:04.237
counts come from the project.
